# To review is one list in three sections, by how far the viewer has got with each PR: those
# they haven't reviewed, those they're part way through, and those they've approved. The
# fixtures hold no reviews of the viewer's, so every PR waits in the first section.
wait settled
open lists
expect text "Mine (19)" exists
expect AXHeading "To review (13)" in list 2 exists
expect button ~"atrium #2928" in list 2 exists
expect list count 2
snap review-columns

# The other two sections follow the first's PRs, each saying it's empty.
scroll list 2 down 20000
wait until AXHeading "Approved (0)" in list 2 exists
expect AXHeading "Reviewing (0)" in list 2 exists
expect text "Nothing here" in list 2 count 2
snap review-columns-end

# Mine and To review share the window evenly until the divider between them is dragged, which
# saves Mine's share of the width; neither goes narrower than 280pt.
expect #lists-divider has value "50"
drag #lists-divider left 288
expect #lists-divider has value "30"
snap lists-resized
drag #lists-divider left 2000
expect #lists-divider has value "19"
drag #lists-divider right 4000
expect #lists-divider has value "81"
